@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `fees-regulations`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- ===========================================================================
-- law-commencement.l4 — section 63 of the Law: תחילה ותחולה.
--
-- Hebrew copied from law.wiki (Wikisource rev 2947808), compared by eye with
-- Sefer HaChukim 3349 (14 January 2025), p. 197.
--
-- 63.(א) תחילתו של חוק זה, למעט פרק ו׳ –
--   (1) לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק
--       המנוי בתוספת הרביעית, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים
--       מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 59, לפי המאוחר (להלן –
--       יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את
--       התוספת הרביעית;
--   (2) לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר שאינו
--       כאמור בפסקה (1) – 18 חודשים מיום התחילה.
--    (ב) תחילתו של פרק ו׳ 18 חודשים מיום התחילה או במועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות
--       לפי סעיף 46, לפי המאוחר.
--
-- The Fourth Schedule (the list of flammable refrigerants) is outside this
-- encoding's scope: whether a system's refrigerant is on it is recorded on
-- the System, not computed.
--
-- COUNTING. "שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו" and "18 חודשים מיום התחילה" are periods
-- of months from a day, so Interpretation Law s 10(b) counts them (its unit is
-- months; il-interpretation-time.l4 reads a "from" period of months as (b),
-- that module's fork F1). Each ends on the day whose number is the starting
-- day's, inside the period. The Law commences ON that last day (fork F32).
-- s 10(c) is not applied to these commencement periods (fork F31); the
-- reading that applies it is offered below for comparison and used nowhere.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 63 — commencement and application`

-- "שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו": Sefer HaChukim 3349 is dated 14 January 2025.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1); SH 3349, 14.1.2025
GIVETH A DATE
`the day this Law was published` MEANS YMD 2025 1 14

@ref Law s 63(a)(1); Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVETH A DATE
`three months from the day this Law was published` MEANS
    `s 10 — the last day of a period of` 3 `months from the day` `the day this Law was published`

-- "מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי סעיף 59": the Fees Regulations, made under
-- ss. 59 and 60, in force on 16 July 2025 (their reg 5). Wikisource's own
-- note at s. 63 says the same: "תחילתן של התקנות לפי סעיף 59, היא ביום 16.7.2025".
@ref Law s 63(a)(1); Fees Regulations reg 5
GIVETH A DATE
`the day regulations under section 59 came into force` MEANS
    `the day the Regulations as made came into force`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- "יום התחילה", the commencement day: the later of the two.
@ref Law s 63(a)(1), "(להלן – יום התחילה)"
GIVETH A DATE
`the commencement day` MEANS
    `the later of` `three months from the day this Law was published` `and` `the day regulations under section 59 came into force`

-- "18 חודשים מיום התחילה": s 10(b), eighteen months from 16 July 2025.
@ref Law s 63(a)(2); Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVETH A DATE
`eighteen months from the commencement day` MEANS
    `s 10 — the last day of a period of` 18 `months from the day` `the commencement day`

-- THE READING NOT TAKEN (fork F31), kept so that the difference is visible:
-- s 10(c) applied to a commencement period, which would move a commencement
-- that falls on a day of rest to the next day that is not one. Nothing in this
-- encoding calls it except the test that shows the two readings apart.
@ref Law s 63(a)(2); Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c) — the reading not taken
GIVEN rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`eighteen months from the commencement day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 18 `months after an event on` `the commencement day` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

-- (a)(1) reaches only a listed flammable refrigerant "whose use has been
-- permitted by any law"; a listed refrigerant not so permitted is "not as
-- stated in paragraph (1)" and falls to (a)(2).
@ref Law s 63(a)(1)-(2)
GIVEN s IS A System
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 63(a)(1) reaches work on` s MEANS
        s's `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule`
    AND s's `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`

@ref Law s 63(a)
GIVEN s IS A System
GIVETH A DATE
`the day this Law, other than Chapter F, comes into force for work on` s MEANS
    IF   `section 63(a)(1) reaches work on` s
    THEN `the commencement day`
    ELSE `eighteen months from the commencement day`

@ref Law s 63(a)
GIVEN w IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Law is in force for` w MEANS
    w's `the day the work is done` AT LEAST `the day this Law, other than Chapter F, comes into force for work on` (w's `the system worked on`)

-- (ב) Chapter F (administrative enforcement) is itself outside this
-- encoding's scope, but s. 63(b) is not. The regulations under s. 46 are not
-- among the sources, so the day they came into force is a fact the caller
-- supplies, or the model declines.
@ref Law s 63(b) — no regulations under s 46 are in the sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the day regulations under section 46 came into force is not in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "the day regulations under section 46 came into force is not in the sources"

@ref Law s 63(b)
GIVEN `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day Chapter F comes into force, given` `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day regulations under section 46 came into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day regulations under section 46 came into force is not in the sources`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN `the later of` `eighteen months from the commencement day` `and` d

-- The power at the end of (a)(1) to amend the Fourth Schedule by order is
-- carried here as text: no order is in the sources, and nothing reads it.
